Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: upstream, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/989975c32db3b547ffc721c53ad35d5089d1e4d1
From 989975c32db3b547ffc721c53ad35d5089d1e4d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:20:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/48] avutil: add multiview and depth information side data

ITU-T H.264 (Annexes G, H and I) and H.265 (Annexes G and I) carry the
information a 3D display or a view synthesizer needs about the views of
a 3D video and the depth pictures that come with them in SEI messages:
multiview scene information (the disparity range), multiview
acquisition information (the intrinsic and extrinsic parameters of the
cameras), multiview view position (the order of the views from left to
right), depth representation information (how depth samples map to Z or
disparity, with the non-linear model of equation G-10), depth timing,
depth sampling information, the constrained depth parameter set
identifier and alternative depth information.

Add a structure for each in multiview.h, keeping the syntax elements as
the messages code them, real numbers included, with a conversion to
double and the table of equation G-10, and a frame side data type for
each.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
Refreshed for FFmpeg 9.1 (deb-multimedia 10:9.1-dmo1), 2026-11-26: the side data values stay as the edition published them in +15: FFmpeg 9.1's AV_FRAME_DATA_DOWNMIX_MATRIX and AV_FRAME_DATA_GAIN_MAP_PARAMS now follow the edition's entries.

